;; PA2z — census slice A: the PERCEIVE and BELIEVE loop-band nodes.
;; R2, R8 (PERCEIVE); R1, R3, R3a, R7 (BELIEVE). 6 nodes x 7 stages = 42 cells.
;;
;; THE HARNESS'S NAIVE ANSWER WAS 42/42 :absent, AND THAT ANSWER IS WRONG TWICE.
;; A uniform result means the instrument is not discriminating, so this slice
;; did not record it. Both errors are stated below with the measurement that
;; found them, because a slice that silently booked 42 absences would have
;; inflated the track's headline deficit by 42 phantom cells.

{:schema :box12/census-slice-v1
 :row :PA2z
 :band :loop
 :stages [:PERCEIVE :BELIEVE]
 :nodes ["R2" "R8" "R1" "R3" "R3a" "R7"]
 :vocabulary "claude-1 approved 2026-09-06: :running-code / :operator-turn / :absent, plus :inapplicable introduced here (see s1)."

 ;; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 :s1-applicability
 {:finding "THE FOUR HANDOFF STAGES ARE INAPPLICABLE TO A NODE THAT NEVER HANDS OFF."
  :argument "commissioned / dispatched / parked / returned describe work being handed to an actor and coming back. R2, R8, R1, R3, R3a and R7 are in-process computations inside one tick; there is no actor to commission and nothing to wait for. Asking whether R2's observation was `dispatched` is a category error, and answering `:absent` books a deficit that does not exist."
  :mechanical-discriminator "A node is handoff-shaped iff its implementation carries handoff conduct. Measured: `rg -l 'dispatch!|/api/alpha/bell|poll-job!' futon2/src/futon2/aif futon2/scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj` returns exactly THREE files in the entire loop tree -- tripwire.clj, actuator_a3.clj, full_loop_runner.clj -- and NO slice-A node appears on any handoff-conduct line (per-node count: 0 for all six). Untruncated; rg -l and rg -c return complete counts."
  :this-is-joes-box-5-ruling-again "Joe, 2026-09-06, on Box 5 (EPIC-run-era.md, 'The rung-ceiling refinement'): formula-transcribed is INAPPLICABLE to pure carrier/record declarations, and 'the no-skipping rule needs a per-kind applicability qualification, MECHANICALLY DERIVED, NOT HAND-WAVED.' Box 12 has the identical defect: it prints a 7-stage denominator for every node without asking whether all seven apply. The discriminator above is the mechanical derivation."
  :split-is-per-stage-not-per-node "Do NOT mark a whole node inapplicable. checked / recorded / surfaced apply to EVERY node -- an in-process computation can still have its output checked, recorded and surfaced, and R2 in fact does have it recorded. Only the four handoff stages are inapplicable. Denominator for a non-handoff node is therefore 3, not 7."
  :effect-on-this-slice "24 of 42 cells are :inapplicable (6 nodes x 4 handoff stages). 18 cells are genuinely censusable and are censused below."
  :proposed-to-claude-1 "As with the :operator-turn vocabulary, :inapplicable is proposed, not retrofitted. ALIGN's 42 adjudicated cells are untouched: R16 and TRACE ARE handoff/record-shaped, and the assurance-band nodes are about assurance conduct, so all seven stages apply to them. This changes no existing verdict."}

 ;; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 :s2-instrument-blind-spot
 {:finding "ALIGN'S NODE-LINK PATTERN HAS A FALSE-NEGATIVE CLASS: node linkage expressed as a FUNCTION-CALL ARGUMENT rather than a literal map entry."
  :measurement "war_machine.clj:5865 defines (route-tag route node via) -> (conj route {:node node :via via :at ...}). The node is a PARAMETER, so the source text at the call sites reads `(route-tag route0 :R2 \"futon2.aif.observation/observe\")` -- :5937 :R2, :6245 :R7, :6246 :R3, :6252 :R8. ALIGN's pattern `(:node|:wm/node|:route/node|:control-node)[[:space:]]+:(R2|R3|R7|R8)` matches ZERO of these: `rg -c` over war_machine.clj returns 0. Meanwhile `rg -o 'route-tag[^)]*:(R[0-9a-z]+)'` enumerates NINE distinct nodes routed this way: R2 R3 R5 R6 R7 R8 R12 R14 R20. Both commands complete; neither is head-limited."
  :second-half-scope "Compounding it, ALIGN's node-link SCOPE is futon3c agency/social/transport, which does not contain war_machine.clj at all -- so even a pattern that matched would not have looked here. The scope is correct for assurance machinery and simply does not reach where loop-band nodes live."
  :NO-ALIGN-VERDICT-CHANGES "Checked before claiming anything. Of the nine route-tagged nodes, only R12 and R20 are censused by ALIGN, and both are marked absent. Their live fixtures agree: 0a18c4f7-R12.edn and 0a18c4f7-R20.edn both carry :status :absent :reason :no-record-field -- the route NAMES them but no record field carries their content. So ALIGN's absent verdict for R12/R20 stands on its own evidence and survives the blind spot. R9 and R10 are not route-tagged at all. NOT an exit-4: no verdict disagrees."
  :why-it-still-matters "PA3z's nodes (R4 R5 R6 R13 R14 R15 R11) include R5, R6 and R14, which ARE route-tagged. Run naively, PA3z would inherit the blind spot and book false absences. Routed to claude-1 as an instrument finding; the harness's pattern is lifted verbatim from ALIGN and this lane will not widen it unilaterally."}

